course: dictionary
lesson: 4928
title: Impatient and waiting
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Impatient describes someone who cannot wait calmly. When things take a long time, an impatient person feels annoyed or restless. «Mia wanted a new game, so she waited three whole impatient months.» The word shows that waiting was hard for her.
explain: Impatient can be used in more than one way. You can be impatient to do something, which means you are very eager to start it soon: «Ella was impatient to open her birthday present.» You can also be impatient with someone, which means you get easily annoyed by them.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Queues, waiting for presents and slow computers are all things that can make someone impatient. To check your meaning, swap in «not able to wait calmly» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Impatient is an adjective: impatient, more impatient, most impatient.
fact: «Impatient» means not able to wait calmly, and easily annoyed when things take time.
fact: «Impatient to» means very eager to do something soon.
fact: «Impatient with» someone means easily annoyed by them.
fact: The prefix im- is used before many words starting with m or p, such as impossible, immature and impatient.
exercise: «Mia waited three whole impatient months.» What does this show about how Mia felt? | She forgot all about the game | She was very rich and did not need it | *She found the waiting hard and could not stay calm | She was asleep for most of the months
exercise: «Ella was impatient to open her birthday present.» What does impatient to mean here? | *Very eager to do something soon | Bored and sleepy | Angry with the present | Unable to read the label
exercise: Which word uses the same im- pattern as impatient? | inside | unhappy | *immature | unkind
test: «Dad was impatient with the slow queue.» What does impatient with mean? | Asleep in the car | Happy to wait in line | *Easily annoyed by the slow queue | Lost in the crowd
test: Which meaning fits «impatient to finish the game»? | Easily annoyed by the game | *Very eager to finish soon | Tired of all games forever | Unable to play any games
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to impatient in «She tapped her foot and sighed at the slow computer»? | calm | sleepy | *restless | happy
